// M0 test room (plan 5.6, style 5.3, 6, 8.1): a 16-bit console room in the spirit of the approved concept (example.png,
// SNES room), the Gate A look-development room of style 27. Room interior 9 x 10 m centered on the origin (x in
// [-4.5, 4.5], z in [-5, 5]); north wall = -Z, doorway in the south wall. Schema:
// src/scene/include/rv/scene/scene_description.hpp.
//
// Composition (style 5.3, 6.1-6.3): the north wall is both the collection wall (two shelf units full of cartridges, the
// floor lamp in the corner) and the hero wall (the CRT on its cabinet with the console, the rug in front of it, an
// armchair turned towards it, a sideboard with a table lamp), under an illuminated "16-BIT CORNER" sign. A 1.2 m wide
// way runs from the doorway to the hero wall between the shelves and the TV corner (the walk scripts of
// tests/input_scripts start on it, --spawn 0,0,3.2,0,-6), and the furniture leaves 1.2 m passages; the south half stays
// open (negative space). Decoration density about 0.4 (style 6.3).
